CNN for Image Classification in MATLAB

Key components:
- imageInputLayer([H W C]) - input size (height, width, channels)
- convolution2dLayer(filterSize, numFilters) - conv layers
- batchNormalizationLayer - speeds up training
- reluLayer - activation function
- maxPooling2dLayer(poolSize, 'Stride', S) - downsampling
- fullyConnectedLayer(outputSize) - dense layer
- dropoutLayer(rate) - prevents overfitting
- softmaxLayer + classificationLayer - output

Training options via trainingOptions():
- 'sgdm' - stochastic gradient descent with momentum
- InitialLearnRate - learning rate
- MaxEpochs - training iterations
- MiniBatchSize - samples per batch
- ValidationData - for monitoring performance
- 'Plots', 'training-progress' - live training plot

Example flow:
1. Load images with imageDatastore
2. Split into train/validation with splitEachLabel
3. Define layer graph
4. Set trainingOptions
5. Call trainNetwork
6. Classify validation set with classify(net, data)
7. Compute accuracy with mean(pred == actual)
